---
title: "Herdr restart B ports: immediate clear epoch, drain earlier effect grants"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Result
    lg1: Restart
    lg2: Breaks NoResumeAfterClear
    lg3: Path to the ClearForgets or NoResumeAfterClear bug
    lg4: Repeats forever, so ClearForgets breaks
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 breaks
  class lg3 bugPath
  class lg4 repeats
  s0: Old session and a queued input
  s1: Seed committed#59; gate holds it
  s2: Restart holds the transition and fence
  s3: Exact close confirmed#59; retire and settle
  s4: Clear requested#59; epoch update pending
  s5: Clear began: epoch bumped#59; restart holds the transition
  s6: Clear discarded the queue#59; restart holds the transition
  s7: Old execution retired#59; a clear overtook the restart
  s8: Exclusion released#59; superseded reply pending
  s9: A launch resumed the conversation a clear ended
  s10: Clear gave up on the transition#59; selector still kept
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: Commit the seed original (acceptance)
  s1 --> s2: Terminate takes transition and fence
  s2 --> s3: Close only the captured pane
  s3 --> s4: User requests clear
  s4 --> s5: Advance epoch and mark clearing, including while old I/O is granted
  s5 --> s6: Clear discards the queue and the launching input
  s5 --> s5: Accept an input into the owner queue
  s6 --> s3: Clear drains earlier grants and tears down their exact session
  s3 --> s7: Retire CAS and settle the old turn
  s7 --> s8: Clear epoch ignored: selector kept
  s8 --> s8: Accept an input into the owner queue
  s8 --> s10: Reply to the command
  s8 --> s9: Owner starts the front: register the launch
